      "id": "s02-carrier",
      "intent": "The carrier equation says the encoder makes a dense feature field from the low-resolution image, then the window operator partitions that field into tokens.",
      "claim": "\\mathbf{F}=\\mathcal{E}(\\mathbf{I}_{\\mathrm{LR}}),\\qquad \\mathbf{X}=\\mathcal{W}(\\mathbf{F})",
      "narration": "The encoder takes the low-resolution image as its input. Its output is the dense feature field, named F in the equation. The window operator acts on that same field. The result is X, a partitioned token representation that keeps every token.",
